    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nOwner deletion is now a soft-delete. The changes:\n\n1. **`Owner` entity** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 added a `deleted` column-mapped field (defaults to `false` for a newly created owner) with `isDeleted()`/`setDeleted(...)`.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `deleted` boolean to the `Owner` response schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it automatically. `GET /api/owners/{id}` now returns `deleted`.\n\n3. **`DeleteOwner`** (the function behind `DELETE /api/owners/{id}`) \u2014 instead of `ownerRepository.delete(owner)`, it now sets `deleted = true` and `save`s, retaining the row. The DELETE pipeline still ends with `RespondWithNoContent` (204, a 2xx), and the owner remains loadable afterward.\n\n4. **`CheckHouseholdUnique`** \u2014 the create endpoint's duplicate/identity check now skips owners flagged `deleted`, so a normally-blocking household duplicate is allowed when the only match has been soft-deleted.\n\n5. **Schema files** (`db/hsqldb`, `db/h2`, `db/mysql`, `db/postgres`) \u2014 added a `deleted BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT FALSE` column so seed inserts and new rows default to not-deleted. (The test profile is `hsqldb,spring-data-jpa` with `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema change is what actually backs the column.)\n\nBoth specified behaviors are verified by the passing acceptance tests: `coreSoftDeleteFlagsAndRetains` (GET shows `deleted:false`, then `true` after DELETE, still 200) and `coreDeletedOwnerIgnoredByDuplicateCheck` (re-creating an identical, soft-deleted owner succeeds). Full suite: `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.",
